{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01042 - MONDO_20543",
  "verbalization": "Melphalan, a chemotherapy agent, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Theca Steroid-producing Cell Malignant Tumor Of Ovary, Not Further Specified through a chain of indications that link it to ovarian tumors. The evidence suggests that Melphalan is associated with Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, which in turn is linked to Tretamine and Carboplatin, both of which are indicated for Theca Steroid-producing Cell Malignant Tumor Of Ovary, Not Further Specified. This indicates a potential pathway where Melphalan may influence the development or progression of ovarian tumors through its interaction with these other drugs. The recurring association between Melphalan and ovarian tumors, particularly those of a steroid-producing nature, suggests a possible role in the treatment or pathogenesis of this malignancy. The integration of these indications highlights a possible mechanism by which Melphalan may contribute to the development of this tumor, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
